<newsitem itemid="633308" id="root" date="1997-06-03" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CTP year share, div rise.</title>
<headline>CTP year share, div rise.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Final shr, (cts)	305.7	 vs 272.3</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 35	    vs 30</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   96.04	 vs 81.39</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   144.19	vs 126.24</p>
<p>    Tax			 46.19	 vs 42.48</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.29	  vs 8.08</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,119.17    vs 965.81</p>
<p>Div payable July 25</p>
<p>on register June 27</p>
<p>Full name: CTP Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The firm it's earnings were diluted slightly by an increased number of shares in issue.</p>
<p>CTP added that a drop in its operating margins due to increased competition in its publishing and printing markets was compensated by good asset management and a strong cash flow.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
